    {
      "id": "s07",
      "title": "Set Up the First Move",
      "vo": "PEN: I sit down to work, then spend ten minutes looking for the right file.\nBUFF: That’s choice architecture. The setup quietly nudges what you do next.\nPEN: If the file is buried and my phone is glowing, the easy move wins.\nBUFF: Don’t make this a willpower audition. Move the phone and open the exact file tonight.\nPEN: I can leave the page, notes, and the tool I need ready on the screen.\nBUFF: Make the helpful action obvious and the detour take a few more steps.\nPEN: That turns tomorrow’s start into doing, rather than searching and deciding.\nBUFF: It’s like loading the bar before the set. Your first rep is waiting.\nPEN: I can also define what finished means, so I don’t drift around the task.\nBUFF: A better setup carries you into a clear finish line. Let’s name one.",
