    {
      "id": "s09",
      "title": "Close the Mental Tab",
      "vo": "PEN: I send the email, then open Sent again because I’m unsure I got it right.\nBUFF: Rechecking can briefly ease uncertainty, but the doubt may return and ask for another look.\nPEN: The same unfinished reply also keeps tapping at my attention during dinner.\nBUFF: Open tasks can linger in your thoughts. A clear plan may help you set them aside.\nPEN: Before checking, I can decide to read the message once carefully, then leave it alone.\nBUFF: For the reply, write the next step and when you’ll do it. Put it outside your head.\nPEN: I don’t have to finish tonight to know where I’ll pick it up tomorrow.\nBUFF: Exactly. The plan is the bookmark. You can stop carrying the whole book around.\nPEN: And starting can be easier when another person knows what I said I’d do.\nBUFF: Let’s make that promise specific and small enough for a real week.",
